   {
    "accessionNumber": "0001193125-26-344912",
    "formType": "8-K",
    "filingDate": "2026-08-11",
    "documentUrl": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/886982/000119312526344912/d179572d8k.htm",
    "summary": "Goldman Sachs filed a Certificate of Elimination for its Series U Preferred Stock following its redemption on August 10, 2026. Concurrently, the company filed a Restated Certificate of Incorporation to include the terms of its newly designated 6.500% Fixed-Rate Reset Non-Cumulative Preferred Stock, Series AA, reflecting these changes.",
    "outputId": "06f1ed1a-1af0-4c70-af6d-8e894b9c4c94"
   },
   {
    "accessionNumber": "0000886982-26-000297",
    "formType": "10-Q",
    "filingDate": "2026-08-03",
    "documentUrl": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/886982/000088698226000297/gs-20260630.htm",
    "summary": "10-Q filing detected. Full financial detail extraction pending (XBRL parsing in follow-up PR).",
    "outputId": null
   },
   {
    "accessionNumber": "0001193125-26-318147",
    "formType": "8-K",
    "filingDate": "2026-07-27",
    "documentUrl": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/886982/000119312526318147/d113214d8k.htm",
    "summary": "Goldman Sachs filed a Certificate of Designations for its new 6.500% Fixed-Rate Reset Non-Cumulative Preferred Stock, Series AA. The issuance of this preferred stock will impose restrictions on GS's ability to pay common stock dividends or repurchase shares if it fails to pay dividends on the Series AA Preferred Stock. This filing, under Item 5.03, formalizes the terms of the new preferred stock and its impact on common shareholders' rights.",
    "outputId": "ff4a9306-2f18-412c-ad18-0cd0d3a0d3f7"
   },
   {
    "accessionNumber": "0001193125-26-310408",
    "formType": "8-K",
    "filingDate": "2026-07-21",
    "documentUrl": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/886982/000119312526310408/d102046d8k.htm",
    "summary": "Goldman Sachs Group Inc. (GS) filed an 8-K to report the issuance of $10 billion in new debt securities on July 21, 2026. This includes $3.5 billion in 5.240% fixed/floating rate notes due 2032, $3.5 billion in 5.655% fixed/floating rate notes due 2037, and $3.0 billion in 6.215% fixed/floating rate notes due 2057. The filing also updated the list of their registered securities, including various preferred stocks and medium-term notes.",
    "outputId": "dd394c2a-03d9-4694-92d3-cf3227caa5d8"
   },
   {
    "accessionNumber": "0001193125-26-308384",
    "formType": "8-K",
    "filingDate": "2026-07-20",
    "documentUrl": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/886982/000119312526308384/d279459d8k.htm",
    "summary": "Goldman Sachs announced a proposed public offering of depositary shares representing interests in a new series of Fixed-Rate Reset Non-Cumulative Preferred Stock, Series AA. Proceeds from this offering are intended to fund the redemption of all outstanding 3.65% Fixed-Rate Reset Non-Cumulative Preferred Stock, Series U, though the offering and redemption are subject to market conditions and other considerations.",
    "outputId": "ed1896d3-414d-4684-b409-28280e6e0880"
   },
   {
    "accessionNumber": "0000886982-26-000294",
    "formType": "8-K",
    "filingDate": "2026-07-14",
    "documentUrl": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/886982/000088698226000294/gs-20260714.htm",
    "summary": "Goldman Sachs Group Inc. (GS) reported its second quarter 2026 earnings on July 14, 2026, which included detailed financial results. The company also disclosed a presentation for a conference call held the same day, discussing its financial performance and outlook. This 8-K includes the press release and presentation as exhibits.",
    "outputId": "ab93416d-fbf8-4be6-88f5-f0a1c0c101b9"
   },
   {
    "accessionNumber": "0001193125-26-281123",
    "formType": "8-K",
    "filingDate": "2026-06-24",
    "documentUrl": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/886982/000119312526281123/d103941d8k.htm",
    "summary": "Goldman Sachs Group Inc. filed an 8-K to announce a press release on June 24, 2026, incorporated as Exhibit 99.1. The filing lists various securities, including common stock, preferred stocks (Series A, C, and D), and several fixed-to-floating rate notes, but does not provide specific details about the content of the press release. The company also confirmed its Chief Financial Officer, Denis P. Coleman III, signed the report.",
    "outputId": "c13fd879-d92d-4987-a89a-8146750952df"
   },
   {
    "accessionNumber": "0001193125-26-255626",
    "formType": "8-K",
    "filingDate": "2026-06-03",
    "documentUrl": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/886982/000119312526255626/d107600d8k.htm",
    "summary": "Goldman Sachs issued $5.0 billion in new debt on June 3, 2026. This offering comprised $2.5 billion of 4.972% Fixed/Floating Rate Notes due 2032 and $2.5 billion of 5.425% Fixed/Floating Rate Notes due 2037.",
    "outputId": "50b10073-4772-4daf-949a-9b10e23f6519"
   },
   {
    "accessionNumber": "0001193125-26-219511",
    "formType": "8-K",
    "filingDate": "2026-05-12",
    "documentUrl": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/886982/000119312526219511/d142159d8k.htm",
    "summary": "Goldman Sachs redeemed all outstanding shares of its 3.80% Fixed-Rate Reset Non-Cumulative Preferred Stock, Series T, on May 10, 2026. The company subsequently filed an amendment to its corporate charter on May 11, 2026, formally eliminating this preferred stock.",
    "outputId": "f7c2bd8a-ee3d-4aaf-bc06-106f6d328f2c"
   },
   {
    "accessionNumber": "0001193125-26-199988",
    "formType": "8-K",
    "filingDate": "2026-05-01",
    "documentUrl": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/886982/000119312526199988/gs-20260429.htm",
    "summary": "At its April 29, 2026 Annual Meeting, Goldman Sachs shareholders elected all 13 nominated directors and approved the advisory vote on executive compensation. Shareholders also rejected three distinct proposals concerning special meeting thresholds, energy supply ratio disclosure, and lobbying disclosure.",
    "outputId": "831ef8dc-6a22-4a19-91ac-d2df4f75c33e"
   },
   {
    "accessionNumber": "0001193125-26-164058",
    "formType": "8-K",
    "filingDate": "2026-04-20",
    "documentUrl": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/886982/000119312526164058/d122102d8k.htm",
    "summary": "Goldman Sachs Group issued $6.5 billion in new debt securities on April 20, 2026, under its shelf registration statement. This issuance comprises $500 million in floating rate notes due 2030, $3 billion in 4.594% fixed/floating rate notes due 2030, and $3 billion in 5.094% fixed/floating rate notes due 2034. The filing includes the legal opinions and consents related to these new securities.",
    "outputId": "3f8aedc0-f307-4242-a0da-5ed0d8f4bf05"
   },
   {
    "accessionNumber": "0000886982-26-000096",
    "formType": "8-K",
    "filingDate": "2026-04-13",
    "documentUrl": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/886982/000088698226000096/gs-20260413.htm",
    "summary": "Goldman Sachs (GS) reported its first quarter 2026 earnings on April 13, 2026. The detailed financial results are available in an accompanying press release (Exhibit 99.1), with a conference call and presentation (Exhibit 99.2) scheduled to discuss the outlook.",
    "outputId": "13f5330b-e7c0-4741-ac2b-d391cb5fa365"
   },
   {
    "accessionNumber": "0001193125-26-105328",
    "formType": "8-K",
    "filingDate": "2026-03-13",
    "documentUrl": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/886982/000119312526105328/gs-20260309.htm",
    "summary": "Lakshmi Mittal is retiring from Goldman Sachs Group Inc.'s Board of Directors, effective at the 2026 Annual Meeting. His departure is in accordance with the Board's age-based retirement policy, which the Board accepted on March 9, 2026.",
    "outputId": "b52a85ba-5f18-4e00-9d9d-6a5f3d6aa0a8"
   }
  ]
